# Credentials & seeded demo accounts
# Untracked 2026-09-13: both files held plaintext passwords for accounts that
# exist in the live database, in a public repository. Kept locally for the demo,
# never committed again.
credentials/
database/seeded-tenant-credentials.json

# Database backups - contain tenant personal data, never commit
backups/

# Presentation working copy. The numbered markdown files and the diagrams are
# COPIES - the originals live in docs/claude_pipeline/outputs/ and
# docs/diagrams/rendered/, and duplicating them in history helps nobody.
#
# The three files that exist only here ARE tracked, because losing them would
# mean losing work: the entry-point note, the HTML script the team films from,
# and the teammate setup guide.
VIDEO PRESENTATION DOCS/*
!VIDEO PRESENTATION DOCS/!! READ THIS FIRST - SEAN.md
!VIDEO PRESENTATION DOCS/filming-script.html
!VIDEO PRESENTATION DOCS/SET UP LOYDS LAPTOP.md
!VIDEO PRESENTATION DOCS/PASTE THIS INTO LOYDS CLAUDE.md
!VIDEO PRESENTATION DOCS/MOTION VIDEO PROMPT.md

# The product video (video/). Its source is committed; what the capture and
# voice scripts regenerate is not - 15 MB of screenshots per run would pile up
# in the history. See video/SCENES.md, "Rebuilding".
video/node_modules/
video/out/
video/public/shots/
video/public/voice/
video/public/sfx/
video/public/score.wav
video/public/pitch/score.wav
video/public/paper/score.wav
video/public/fe-galang-building.webp
video/public/icon-512.png
video/public/floorplans/
video/public/music.mp3

# vite writes these beside the config during a build; they are not source
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*

# Throwaway probe scripts. An audit writes these to attack one endpoint and
# then stops caring about them. Two of them were swept into a commit on
# 2026-09-19 by someone running `git add -A` on the other machine; they read
# `credentials/creds.txt` at runtime and carried no literal secret, so nothing
# leaked, but they should never have been offered to a commit at all.
backend/scripts/tmp-*
scripts/tmp-*

# Local audit harnesses: pages that mount the real app against fixture data
# with a mocked fetch, so a screen can be looked at without a sign-in. Four
# of them sat untracked in frontend/ on 2026-09-25, one `git add -A` away
# from the public repository - the same trap as the probe scripts above.
frontend/_harness-*.html

# Binaries
*.exe

# Field-test screenshots (scripts/field-tests) - may show live pages; not for the repository
scripts/field-tests/shots/

# Raw survey exports carry respondents' names (7 Oct 2026, B-103): keep them off the public repo
/IEC-25010-Software-Quality-Assessment.csv

# Prompt logs for the AI-use disclosure: prompts can quote tenants, and the repo is public
/ai-use-log/

# The course guides (the professor's PDFs) stay on the machine that has them; the repo is public
/docs/FINAL MANUSCRIPT/guides/

# Documents kept on this machine but out of the repository (13 Oct 2026 clean-up); recover any
# of them from the tag pre-cleanup-2026-10-13 on another machine
/_ARCHIVE (not in repo)/

# The AI-use statement and its evidence: ready for the adviser, kept outside the repository (13 Oct 2026)
/_AI_USE (not in repo)/

# AI tool folders (13 Oct 2026): kept on the machine that uses them, not in the repository.
